# COREX — Corext: A LLM From Scratch

**COREX** (Centralized Organized Reasoning & Extraction Matrix) is a complete, self-contained large language model built entirely from scratch. No HuggingFace abstractions, no PyTorch transforms hand-waving — just the raw architecture working code and documentation.

## Architecture

| Component | Detail |
|---|---|
| **Tokenizer** | Byte-level BPE (512 base + 960 merges = 1472 vocab) |
| **Embedding** | Learned embeddings (vocab × dim) |
| **Block** | Causal Transformer with SwiGLU FFN |
| **Attention** | Multi-head RoPE, softmax attention, masked |
| **Norm** | RMSNorm pre-LN |
| **Positional** | Rotary Embeddings (RoPE) |
| **FFN** | SwiGLU gated feed-forward |
| **Init** | Kaiming normal, 0.1 residual scale |

## Quick Start

```bash
pip install corext
corex train --preset 100m
corex generate --checkpoint checkpoints/corex-100m.pth "Hello" --max-tokens 128
```

## Model Zoo

- **corex-100m**: ~100M params, 24 layers, dim=512
- **corex-340m**: ~340M params, 32 layers, dim=768  
- **corex-1b**: ~1B params, 48 layers, dim=1024

## Install

```bash
pip install corext
```

